225→
226→@P = primuv(0, 'P', 0, uv);
227→@N = primuv(1, 'N', 0, uv);
228→```
229→Creates circular motion by using sine and cosine of the frame number to generate UV coordinates, then samples position and normal attributes from primitives using primuv(). The UV values are fitted from the -1 to 1 range into 0.2 to 0.2 (likely meant to be a smaller range) and offset by 0.5 to center them, allowing an object to move in a circular path on a surface while sampling normals for orientation.
