288→Creates circular animation by calculating UV coordinates using sine and cosine of time, fitting the range from -1,1 to -0.2,0.2, then offsetting by 0.5 to center. Uses primuv to sample position and normal from input geometry at the animated UV coordinates, causing the point to orbit around the primitive surface.
