333→Creates circular motion by using sine and cosine of time to generate UV coordinates, fitting them to a constrained range around the center (0.5, 0.5), then sampling position and normal attributes from input 1 at those UV coordinates using primuv. The object moves in a circular path on a surface (grid or NURBS) while maintaining orientation based on the surface normal.
