347→```
348→Creates animated UV coordinates using sine and cosine of time, fits them to a specific range, then samples position and normal attributes from a NURBS surface at those UV coordinates. The circular motion causes an object to orbit on the surface while maintaining orientation based on the surface normal, though orientation can fluctuate as the frame of reference shifts.
349→
