610→```
611→Uses xyzdist() to find the closest point on geometry from input 1, storing the resulting primitive ID in @prim1d and UV coordinates in @uv. The function returns the distance which is stored in @dist. Note that UV sampling requires a separate function (uvsample), and this demonstrates how primitive-based geometry like tubes, spheres, and discs have their own UV space calculations.
