620→```
621→Demonstrates using xyzdist() on non-polygonal primitive surfaces like tubes, spheres, and discs to compute UV coordinates. When geometry lacks explicit UVs, Houdini renderers use per-face UV coordinates calculated through primitive intrinsics, which is why default grids show tiled textures per face.
