628→@Cd = v;
629→@dist;
630→
631→@dist = xyzdist(1, @P, @primid, @uv);
632→```
633→The xyzdist() function finds the closest point on a geometry and returns the distance, while also writing the primitive ID and UV coordinates to output variables. This is a powerful complement to primuv() - where primuv() retrieves attributes given a UV location, xyzdist() finds the UV location of the nearest surface point.
