705→## primuv Sampling
706→
707→### xyzdist and primuv combined lookup [[Ep8, 52:00](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KJUZD4PTyz0&t=3120s)]
708→```vex
709→int @primid;
710→vector @uv;
711→float @dist;
712→
713→@dist = xyzdist(1, @P, @primid, @uv);
714→
715→@P = primuv(1, "P", @primid, @uv);
716→```
717→Uses xyzdist() to find the closest point on a surface (input 1), which returns the distance, primitive ID, and UV coordinates. Then uses primuv() to look up the actual position at those UV coordinates, effectively snapping points to the closest location on the target surface.
718→
719→### Transferring Attributes with primuv [[Ep8, 53:00](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KJUZD4PTyz0&t=3180s)]
720→```vex
