741→@Cd = primuv(1, 'Cd', @primid, @uv);
742→```
743→After using xyzdist() to find the closest point on a geometry and get its primitive ID and UV coordinates, primuv() can be used to sample not just position but also other attributes like color. This demonstrates how to transfer color (@Cd) from a source geometry to points by sampling at the closest UV location.
