754→@Cd = primuv(1, 'Cd', @primid, @uv);
755→```
756→This code finds the nearest point on a reference geometry using xyzdist() to get the primitive ID and UV coordinates, then uses primuv() to both relocate the point position and transfer the color attribute from the reference geometry. This technique allows points to inherit both position and color from a surface while maintaining parametric UV relationships.
